 "_about": "Public-domain David James Burrell (1844-1926), Reformed Church in America minister of the Marble Collegiate Church, New York, for the Word Hoard: his thirty-odd volumes of sermons, expositions and apologetics, from The Religions of the World (1888) and The Gospel of Gladness (1892) through The Cloister Book (1909), The Old-Time Religion and The Sermon, its Construction and Delivery (1913), The Apostles' Creed (1915), Why I Believe the Bible (1917), Paul's Campaigns, Companions and Letters (1918-1921) and Life and Letters of St. Paul (1925) to The Golden Parable (1926). Texts are from Internet Archive scans. Added 2026-10-23 by lane A, round 76 (my pick); Adam may veto the whole shelf. Every printing dated before 1930, so public domain in the US. No uids minted.",
